      en: "Taitung is a coastal city in southeastern Taiwan, capital of Taitung County. It is known for its indigenous culture, scenic beauty, and relaxed atmosphere. The city has a population of about 100,000 and an area of 109 km². Taitung's economy relies on tourism, agriculture (rice, betel nuts), and fisheries. Key landmarks include Taitung Forest Park, Liyu Lake, and the Taitung Railway Art Village. The city is served by Taitung Station and Taitung Airport. Annual events like the Taitung Hot Air Balloon Festival and the Amis Harvest Festival draw many visitors. Taitung also promotes eco-friendly initiatives and sustainable development.",
