      en: "Huwei is a city in Yunlin County, western Taiwan. It has a population of about 70,000 and an area of 48 km². Huwei is an agricultural center for rice, sugarcane, and vegetables. The city hosts the Huwei Industrial Park. The economy relies on agriculture, food processing, and light manufacturing. Key landmarks include Huwei Temple and Huwei Park. An annual Sugarcane Festival is held. The city is served by Huwei Station on the Western Line. Huwei is known for its traditional sweets and rural charm.",
